cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fanbase, please cite it as below."
title: "Fanbase: a registry of Fandango input specifications"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Fandango Fuzzer Team"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fandango-fuzzer/fanbase"
url: "https://github.com/fandango-fuzzer/fanbase"
abstract: >-
  Fanbase is a collection of Fandango input specifications (grammars) for image, video, audio and
  other file formats, from which thousands of random test inputs can be produced. This repository is
  the registry; the fanbase command that browses and installs from it is fanbase-cli.
keywords:
  - fuzzing
  - test generation
  - grammars
  - file formats
  - Fandango
